  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Starting several sampling chains with invalid input should produce a useful error. An annotation prevented two error-handling methods from being defined. Moving it inside the methods restores the intended error.",
          "refs": [
            "pr",
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The change affects validation when starting several chains with initial_params or initial_state. A valid sampler setup should behave as before. This review follows one invalid state through the public sample call, then checks the intended error.",
          "refs": [
            "pr",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "group": "overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "purpose",
      "title": "Missing validation methods",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A fallback is the method used when no more specific input type matches. Here it should reject an unsupported initial value with ArgumentError. @nospecialize tells Julia not to specialize on input types. It must be inside these method bodies.",
          "refs": [
            "pr",
            "julia-issue",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Julia issue 49512 explains why @nospecialize around a function definition can consume it. This PR places the annotation inside each fallback.",
          "refs": [
            "pr",
            "julia-issue",
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nothing uses the default. AbstractArray inputs are checked against nchains. Other types reach an ArgumentError naming initial_params or initial_state.",
          "refs": [
            "head-fallbacks",
            "serial",
            "threads",
            "distributed"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "group": "overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "behavior",
      "title": "Before and after",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This example asks for four serial chains and passes an integer as their initial state. That integer is invalid. The call should explain the required input before the sampler starts.",
          "refs": [
            "serial",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "title": "Invalid initial state",
          "language": "julia",
          "code": "using AbstractMCMC, Random\nstruct ProbeModel <: AbstractMCMC.AbstractModel end\nstruct ProbeSampler <: AbstractMCMC.AbstractSampler end\nsample(MersenneTwister(42), ProbeModel(), ProbeSampler(),\n       MCMCSerial(), 3, 4; progress=false, initial_state=10)"
        },
        {
          "type": "compare",
          "title": "Unsupported initial_state = 10",
          "before": "Base 418afe0: MethodError from check_initial_state(::Int64, ::Int64). The generic fallback method is absent.",
          "after": "Head 3aac86b: ArgumentError: initial_state must be specified as a vector of length equal to the number of chains or `nothing`. The generic fallback method exists.",
          "refs": [
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "All six invalid calls across MCMCSerial, MCMCThreads and MCMCDistributed changed from MethodError to ArgumentError. No sampler step ran. The second case used initial_params=(a=1.0, b=2.0)."
        }
      ],
      "group": "changes"
    },
    {
      "id": "design",
      "title": "Validation calls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read the path from sample to the serial ensemble. It first validates initial_params, then initial_state. With the default parameters and integer state used above, the state fallback throws before any sampler step runs.",
          "refs": [
            "serial",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "id": "serial-validation",
          "title": "initial_state rejection",
          "direction": "LR",
          "text": "MCMCSerial path for integer initial_state and default initial_params. Other default ensembles use the same validators.",
          "refs": [
            "sample-rng",
            "serial",
            "threads",
            "distributed",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ],
          "nodes": [
