                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nothing keeps the default. An AbstractArray uses the length-checking method. Other types need the generic fallback restored by this PR. Threads and distributed ensembles call the same validators.",
          "refs": [
            "head-fallbacks",
            "threads",
            "distributed"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "group": "design"
    },
    {
      "id": "review-actions",
      "title": "Review",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "diff",
          "title": "Define the fallback",
          "text": "The PR changes initial_params and initial_state this way. The public probe covers both.",
          "path": "src/sample.jl",
          "before": "@nospecialize check_initial_params(x, n) = throw(\n    ArgumentError(\n        \"initial_params must be specified as a vector of length equal to the number of chains or `nothing`\",\n    ),\n)\ncheck_initial_params(::Nothing, n) = nothing\n",
          "after": "function check_initial_params(x, n)\n    @nospecialize\n    throw(\n        ArgumentError(\n            \"initial_params must be specified as a vector of length equal to the number of chains or `nothing`\",\n        ),\n    )\nend\ncheck_initial_params(::Nothing, n) = nothing\n",
          "scope": "pr",
          "verification": "tested",
          "refs": [
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "finding",
          "status": "verified",
          "title": "Validation result",
          "text": "Both fallback methods exist on head. Invalid public calls produce ArgumentError instead of MethodError. The serial controls accept nothing and matching arrays.",
          "refs": [
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks",
            "new-tests"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The current PR title and body are already concise.",
          "refs": [
            "pr"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prompt",
          "title": "Check the fallback",
          "text": "Use the public API on both revisions.",
          "instructions": "Run examples/abstractmcmc-222.jl on the exact base and head. Check invalid initial_state and initial_params across all three default ensembles, then the serial controls. Confirm invalid inputs fail before sampling. Report Julia and package revisions.",
          "refs": [
            "base-fallbacks",
            "head-fallbacks",
            "serial",
            "threads",
            "distributed"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "group": "review"
    },
